<span class="cat-badge">Guide &middot; Trips</span>
<h1>Hanoi to Cat Ba by Motorbike: Luggage Packing Guide</h1>
<p>Packing for Cat Ba is packing for a chain, a long flat corridor, a scheduled crossing and an island with a park on its spine, and each link asks the luggage a different question. The corridor asks whether the load is stable at steady speed, the ferry asks whether everything important is dry and on your person, and the island asks whether the machine is light enough for slow, climbing, crowd-shaped roads with a beach town at the end of them. This guide answers in order: what to bring, where to put it, how to keep it dry, and what to check at the counter, without inventing a single item the sea has not requested.</p>
<p>The machine and its luggage advice come from Motorbike Rental - Nguyen Tu, 112 Nguyen Van Cu in Long Bien, Hanoi, open daily 09:00 to 21:00, where the desk briefs riders daily on loading machines for the island chain. Start at the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-trips/">Hanoi motorbike trips</a> hub, study the parent <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-trips/long-distance-motorbike-trip-planning/">long-distance motorbike trip planning</a> guide, see the machines and terms on the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental/">Hanoi motorbike rental</a> page, review the <a href="/motorbike-guides/">motorbike guides</a> for riding and safety, and keep <a href="/renting-a-motorbike-in-vietnam/">renting a motorbike in Vietnam</a> open for the legal layer.</p>
